# Refactoring Standards

Apply these standards when refactoring code.

<red_lines>
- Run tests before starting. Run tests after every step. If a test breaks, the refactor is wrong — stop and revert.
- One refactoring pattern per logical change. Never mix refactoring with feature changes.
- Preserve all existing behavior — refactoring changes structure, not function.
- Prefer small, safe transformations over large rewrites.

<!-- @import _core/4_refactoring/smell_detection/redlines.md -->
</red_lines>

<execution_protocol>
**Interlock**: For complex restructuring, you MUST delegate to `/refactor` to produce a structured refactoring plan before executing changes.

<!-- @import _core/4_refactoring/smell_detection/protocol.md -->
